<title>QATAR: Qatar National Bank details 96 results, bonus issue.</title>
<headline>Qatar National Bank details 96 results, bonus issue.</headline>
<dateline>DOHA 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>				    (million riyals)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   329.72    vs   289.04</p>
<p>    Net interest income		453.40    vs   391.09</p>
<p>    Other income			  72.60    vs    81.30</p>
<p>    Provision for loan losses	 27.00    vs    55.22</p>
<p>    Total dividend		     110.74    vs    88.59</p>
<p>    Total assets (billion riyals)   16.28    vs    17.22</p>
<p>    Shareholders equity (billion)    2.66    vs     2.44</p>
<p>Full name: Qatar National Bank Ltd</p>
<p>Note: The Qatar government owns half of QNB. The rest is held by Qatari citizens. The board agreed to the payment of a cash dividend equal to 25 percent of the capital and the issue of bonus shares on the basis of one for every four held.</p>
</text>
